{"title": "8. Tafkhīm and Tarqīq – Heavy and Light", "intro": "Tafkhīm is fullness of sound (the back of the tongue rises and the sound fills the mouth); tarqīq is thinness. The seven istiʿlāʾ letters are always heavy; ر and the lām of الله vary; all other letters are always light (including alif, which follows the letter before it).", "rules": [
 {"name": "Levels of tafkhīm in istiʿlāʾ letters", "arabic": "مراتب التفخيم",
  "text": "Strongest → weakest: (1) with fatḥah followed by alif, (2) with fatḥah, (3) with ḍammah, (4) sākin, (5) with kasrah. The letters of iṭbāq (ص ض ط ظ) are heavier than غ خ ق at each level.",
  "examples": [(79, 34, ["الطامة"]), (2, 7, ["ختم"]), (2, 27, ["ويقطعون"]), (6, 7, ["قرطاس"])]},
 {"name": "Rāʾ with tafkhīm (heavy)", "arabic": "تفخيم الراء",
  "text": "ر is heavy when: (a) it has fatḥah or ḍammah; (b) it is sākin after fatḥah or ḍammah; (c) it is sākin after a kasrah that is temporary (hamzat al-waṣl) or that belongs to the previous word; (d) it is sākin after kasrah and followed in the same word by an istiʿlāʾ letter with fatḥah (قِرْطَاس، فِرْقَة، مِرْصَاد، إِرْصَاد); (e) stopping on it when preceded by fatḥah/ḍammah, or by a sākin (other than yāʾ) preceded by fatḥah/ḍammah.",
  "examples": [(1, 2, ["رب"]), (1, 1, ["الرحمن"]), (89, 28, ["ارجعي"]), (23, 99, ["رب", "ارجعون"]), (6, 7, ["قرطاس"]), (9, 122, ["فرقة"]), (78, 21, ["مرصادا"]), (89, 1, ["والفجر"])]},
 {"name": "Rāʾ with tarqīq (light)", "arabic": "ترقيق الراء",
  "text": "ر is light when: (a) it has kasrah; (b) it is sākin after an original kasrah and not followed by an istiʿlāʾ letter in the same word; (c) stopping on it when preceded by kasrah, or by yāʾ sākinah, or by a sākin preceded by kasrah. Note: وَٱلْفَجْرِ (89:1) stopped upon is *light* — the ر follows a sākin jīm that itself follows a kasrah.",
  "examples": [(2, 49, ["فرعون"]), (2, 3, ["رزقنهم"]), (2, 234, ["خبير"]), (89, 1, ["والفجر"]), (2, 17, ["بنورهم"]), (114, 1, ["برب"])]},
 {"name": "Rāʾ with two permitted readings", "arabic": "الراء التي يجوز فيها الوجهان",
  "text": "Both tafkhīm and tarqīq are transmitted for Ḥafṣ in: فِرْقٍ (26:63, because the istiʿlāʾ letter after it has kasrah); and when stopping on مِصْرَ (10:87, 12:21, 12:99, 43:51 – tafkhīm preferred, since the sākin ṣād is an istiʿlāʾ letter), ٱلْقِطْرِ (34:12 – tarqīq preferred), نُذُرِ (54:16 etc.), يَسْرِ (89:4), أَسْرِ (11:81, 26:52) and فَأَسْرِ (15:65, 44:23) — in these last, tarqīq is preferred because of the deleted yāʾ.",
  "examples": [(26, 63, ["فرق"]), (34, 12, ["القطر"]), (54, 16, ["ونذر"]), (89, 4, ["يسر"]), (10, 87, ["بمصر"])]},
 {"name": "Lām of the name Allāh (lām al-jalālah)", "arabic": "لام لفظ الجلالة",
  "text": "The lām of ٱللَّه is heavy (tafkhīm) when preceded by fatḥah or ḍammah, and light (tarqīq) when preceded by kasrah. All other lāms in the Qur'an are light.",
  "examples": [(110, 1, ["نصر", "الله"]), (112, 1, ["هو", "الله"]), (1, 1, ["بسم", "الله"]), (1, 2, ["الحمد", "لله"]), (2, 255, ["الله"])]},
]},
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
{"title": "9. The Lām of ال (Definite Article)", "intro": "The lām of the definite article ال is either pronounced clearly or merged into the following letter.", "rules": [
 {"name": "Lām Qamariyyah (moon lām) – pronounced", "arabic": "اللام القمرية",
  "text": "Before the 14 letters ابغ حجك وخف عقيمه (ا ب غ ح ج ك و خ ف ع ق ي م هـ) the lām is pronounced with sukūn. The mushaf writes a sukūn on it.",
  "examples": [(1, 2, ["الحمد", "العلمين"]), (54, 1, ["القمر"]), (2, 3, ["بالغيب"]), (2, 4, ["وبالءاخرة"])]},
 {"name": "Lām Shamsiyyah (sun lām) – merged", "arabic": "اللام الشمسية",
  "text": "Before the other 14 letters (ت ث د ذ ر ز س ش ص ض ط ظ ل ن) the lām is silent and merged into the next letter, which carries a shaddah. The mushaf leaves the lām without any mark.",
  "examples": [(1, 1, ["الرحمن", "الرحيم"]), (1, 6, ["الصرط"]), (114, 1, ["الناس"]), (91, 1, ["والشمس"]), (2, 6, ["الذين"])]},
]},
