{"title": "10. Idghām of Two Letters (General)", "intro": "Beyond nūn and mīm, any two adjacent letters where the first is sākin may merge depending on how similar they are. This is ṣaghīr (minor) idghām — the first letter is sākin and the second voweled.", "rules": [
 {"name": "Idghām Mutamāthilayn (identical letters)", "arabic": "إدغام المتماثلين",
  "text": "Two identical letters, the first sākin: the first merges completely into the second. Exception: if the first is a madd letter (و after ḍammah, ي after kasrah) it is *not* merged, e.g. قَالُوا۟ وَ… , فِي يَوْمٍ.",
  "examples": [(2, 60, ["اضرب", "بعصاك"]), (5, 61, ["وقد", "دخلوا"]), (4, 78, ["يدرككم"]), (21, 87, ["إذ", "ذهب"]), (27, 28, ["اذهب", "بكتبي"]), (2, 16, ["ربحت", "تجرتهم"])]},
 {"name": "Idghām Mutajānisayn (same makhraj, different attributes)", "arabic": "إدغام المتجانسين",
  "text": "Letters from the same makhraj: ت→ط, ت→د, د→ت, ط→ت, ذ→ظ, ث→ذ, ب→م. Ḥafṣ merges them. When ط merges into ت (بَسَطتَ، أَحَطتُ، فَرَّطتُمْ), the merging is *nāqiṣ* – the heaviness (iṭbāq) of ط remains audible. The mushaf writes the second letter with shaddah (or leaves the first bare where nāqiṣ).",
  "examples": [(3, 72, ["وقالت", "طائفة"]), (7, 189, ["أثقلت", "دعوا"]), (5, 28, ["بسطت"]), (27, 22, ["أحطت"]), (12, 80, ["فرطتم"]), (7, 176, ["يلهث", "ذلك"]), (4, 64, ["إذ", "ظلموا"]), (11, 42, ["اركب", "معنا"]), (2, 256, ["قد", "تبين"])]},
 {"name": "Idghām Mutaqāribayn (close makhraj / attributes)", "arabic": "إدغام المتقاربين",
  "text": "Ḥafṣ merges in two cases only: ق→ك in أَلَمْ نَخْلُقكُّم (77:20) – idghām is complete per the Shāṭibiyyah (the qāf's heaviness disappears); and ل→ر as in قُل رَّبِّ, بَل رَّفَعَهُ. (Nūn sākinah with ل ر ي م و is also mutaqāribayn/mutajānisayn, covered in Section 4.)",
  "examples": [(77, 20, ["نخلقكم"]), (23, 118, ["وقل", "رب"]), (4, 158, ["بل", "رفعه"])]},
]},
