{"title": "11. Hamzah, Hamzat al-Waṣl, and Silent Letters", "intro": "Rules for beginning a word, for the hamzah, and for letters written but not pronounced.", "rules": [
 {"name": "Hamzat al-Waṣl (connecting hamzah)", "arabic": "همزة الوصل",
  "text": "Written as alif with a small ṣād-head (ٱ). Pronounced only when *starting* on the word, dropped when joining. With ال it takes fatḥah. In verbs: ḍammah if the third letter has an original ḍammah (ٱدْخُلُوا۟), otherwise kasrah (ٱقْرَأْ، ٱسْتَغْفِرْ). In the seven nouns (ٱسْم، ٱبْن، ٱبْنَة، ٱمْرُؤ، ٱمْرَأَة، ٱثْنَيْن، ٱثْنَتَيْن) it takes kasrah.",
  "examples": [(96, 1, ["اقرأ", "باسم"]), (2, 58, ["ادخلوا"]), (2, 2, ["الكتب"]), (110, 3, ["واستغفره"]), (96, 3, ["اقرأ"])]},
 {"name": "Two hamzahs together: Ḥafṣ reads both fully", "arabic": "تحقيق الهمزتين",
  "text": "Where two hamzahs meet in one word (e.g. أَأَنذَرْتَهُمْ), Ḥafṣ pronounces both with full taḥqīq (no tas-hīl, no inserted alif), unlike several other readers. Across two words (e.g. جَآءَ أَحَدٌ) both are also fully pronounced.",
  "examples": [(2, 6, ["ءأنذرتهم"]), (4, 43, ["جاء", "أحد"]), (13, 5, ["أءذا", "أءنا"])]},
 {"name": "Silent letters marked with a small round circle", "arabic": "الحروف الزائدة رسماً",
  "text": "A round circle (۟) over a letter means it is written but never pronounced, whether joining or stopping: the alif after wāw al-jamāʿah (قَالُوا۟), the wāw in أُو۟لَٰٓئِكَ, the alif in مِا۟ئَة, the yāʾ in أَفَإِي۟ن.",
  "examples": [(2, 11, ["قالوا"]), (2, 5, ["أولئك"]), (2, 259, ["مائة"]), (3, 144, ["أفإين"])]},
 {"name": "Letters silent in joining but pronounced at a stop (small oval)", "arabic": "الألف المقيدة بالوصل",
  "text": "An oval (۠) marks a letter dropped when continuing but read when stopping: the alif of أَنَا۠ (I), and the alifs of ٱلظُّنُونَا۠ (33:10), ٱلرَّسُولَا۠ (33:66), ٱلسَّبِيلَا۠ (33:67), قَوَارِيرَا۠ (76:15), لَٰكِنَّا۠ (18:38). In سَلَٰسِلَا۟ (76:4) Ḥafṣ may stop either with the alif or without it; joining is always without.",
  "examples": [(2, 258, ["أنا", "أحي"]), (33, 10, ["الظنونا"]), (33, 66, ["الرسولا"]), (76, 15, ["قواريرا"]), (76, 4, ["سلسلا"]), (18, 38, ["لكنا"])]},
 {"name": "Small (added) letters – pronounced though not in the base script", "arabic": "الحروف المحذوفة رسماً الملحقة",
  "text": "Letters omitted from the Uthmani script but read are written small: the dagger alif (ٰ) in ٱلصَّلَوٰة, ٱلرَّحْمَٰن, ذَٰلِكَ; the small wāw in دَاوُۥد; the small yāʾ in إِبْرَٰهِـۧمَ; the small nūn in نُـۨجِى (21:88).",
  "examples": [(2, 3, ["الصلوة"]), (2, 251, ["داود"]), (2, 124, ["إبرهم"]), (21, 88, ["نجي"]), (2, 2, ["ذلك"])]},
]},
